From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] buttons: reboot BMC after a physical UID hold of five seconds

Use the existing UID GPIO owner and its monotonic sd-event loop. A short
press retains the standard Released signal and identify-LED handler. A
continuous five-second hold requests an orderly BMC reboot once, consumes
the long release, and does not drive the host power/reset outputs. Recheck
the input before reboot and ignore a release already held at daemon startup.
Base: phosphor-buttons 9827866ef17c13bb9de5f492639a02d4a8e58f88.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD UID button policy]

diff --git a/inc/id_button.hpp b/inc/id_button.hpp
--- a/inc/id_button.hpp
+++ b/inc/id_button.hpp
@@ -25,6 +25,8 @@
 
 #include <unistd.h>
 
+#include <cstdint>
+
 #include <phosphor-logging/elog-errors.hpp>
 
 static constexpr auto ID_BUTTON = "ID_BTN";
@@ -47,6 +49,7 @@
 
     ~IDButton()
     {
+        cancelLongPressTimer();
         deInit();
     }
 
@@ -62,4 +65,16 @@
     }
 
     void handleEvent(sd_event_source* es, int fd, uint32_t revents) override;
+
+  private:
+    static constexpr uint64_t longPressUsec = 5ULL * 1000000;
+    sd_event_source* longPressTimer = nullptr;
+    int pressedFd = -1;
+    bool buttonPressed = false;
+    bool rebootRequested = false;
+
+    void startLongPressTimer(int fd);
+    void cancelLongPressTimer();
+    static int longPressExpired(sd_event_source* source, uint64_t usec,
+                                void* userdata);
 };
diff --git a/src/id_button.cpp b/src/id_button.cpp
--- a/src/id_button.cpp
+++ b/src/id_button.cpp
@@ -15,6 +15,11 @@
